{"title":"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #18</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #21</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangular prism has a volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4d0902367198ebad8ccd35b7dada7d88eb16d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 cm^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />. Two edges of the triangular prism measure 3 cm and 4 cm, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The height of the prism, in cm, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4a1ddad7412d24f3b321734fa3eee0da2ad93b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 10 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 16 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of the triangular prism will be the area of the base multiplied by its height.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of the base and the height, respectively. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7dd75eaa716f54b141f5f84dbf1462c45f5a833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{3 cm * 4 cm}{2} = 6 cm^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"191\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/286f03e4f4ac607e7d8ad91e43e96cfd3e99d111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A * h = V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/5/305dc64a077ef50dca39efad1fa0507430095888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 cm^2 * h = 120 cm^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"153\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9ab30e532eb2b4ee1955bd8e999a71cfbfc0717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\frac{120 cm^3}{6 cm^2} = 20 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/82393721d31614209850e60a681a87495b01f738.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.ph